On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:36:07 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> One more revision to this... I do want to have an explicit sync dir
> list. It should just be INBOX ARCHIVE lists.

Done in "[PATCH v8 0/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's
mail hub" [1]. Only patch 9 changed, now titled "[PATCH v8 9/9]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Deliver posts to INBOX and sync it" [2]:

- mbsyncrc has "Patterns INBOX Archive lists", and mbsync syncs no
  other folder. I took ARCHIVE to mean the folder Archive, Fastmail's
  archive folder, since IMAP folder names are case-sensitive.
- Posts still land in INBOX, and INBOX is still in the maildir.
- Dovecot creates lists again beside Archive, so all three exist on
  lab-mail from the start. mbsync is back to Create None, and its
  ACL entry loses the create right it needed for Patterns *.
- The Fastmail rule that files into lists can still go once this is
  on the jail. The mail already in lists stays on the list.

The interdiff against v7 is in the cover letter. mbsync 1.5.1 parses
the new mbsyncrc. Dovecot and smtpd are not installed here, so it was
not run on a jail.

